8. ARTICLE PROCESSING PIPELINE

Implement the following processing pipeline:

Fetch articles from configured sources.
Validate and normalize incoming data.
Convert timestamps to a consistent format while displaying local time appropriately.
Normalize URLs and source names.
Remove exact duplicates.
Detect near-duplicate articles.
Classify articles by topic and geography.
Match related reports to existing events.
Generate AI summaries where permitted.
Calculate an importance score.
Determine whether a story meets breaking-news criteria.
Store the processed article and associated metadata.
Update category feeds and event timelines.
Record processing status and errors.

Make processing idempotent so rerunning a job does not create duplicate articles, summaries, or events.

Use scheduled background jobs and provider-aware refresh intervals.

Prioritize breaking-news sources for more frequent updates while keeping less time-sensitive categories on a reasonable schedule.

Do not run continuous polling in a user's browser or repeatedly fetch all sources on every page load.

Respect API quotas, rate limits, provider terms, caching rules, and robots or access restrictions where applicable.

Implement exponential backoff for transient errors and avoid repeated retries of permanent failures.

